\fs24 \cf0 Step 1: The decoder's job, derived from scratch
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
What only the decoder can do. It has to turn one chunk-level plan plus 63 tokens of local context into a distribution over the next token.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The "unrolling" problem. One plan \uc0\u265 _\{j+1\} arrives at the start of a chunk and has to produce 4 tokens. Each of those positions already knows a different number of the chunk's tokens. What does that imply?\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Where the information comes from. What part of p(x_\{t+1\}) can come from 
\f4\fs26 tok
\f1\fs24 , what part only from the plan, and what that means for the loss.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The bypass audit. Every route by which the decoder could reach the loss without the core, and how each gets closed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

