\f3\b\fs36 \cf0 1. The mixer: derived from reach\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Reach.
\f1\b0  The reach of a state at position t is the farthest token x_\{t\uc0\u8722 r\} that can change it. In the encoder, 
\f4\fs26 tok
\f1\fs24  has reach 63. Everything more than 63 tokens back must reach the decoder through the plan (the use principle).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
FULL attention:
\f1\b0  position t attends to every earlier j, so the reach is the whole past. That's F6.\
\ls11\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Linear attention
\f1\b0  (GDN, Mamba, RetNet). The state is a running memory\uc0\u8232 $$S_t = \\alpha_t, S_\{t-1\} + k_t v_t^\{\\top\}$$\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
S_t is a d\'d7d matrix.\
\ls11\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\uc0\u945 _t 
\f9 \uc0\u8712 
\f1  (0,1] is a learned decay.\
\ls11\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
k_t v_t
\f2 \uc0\u7488 
\f1  writes token t's key\'96value pair into the memory.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Unrolling it gives $S_t = \\sum_j \\big(\\prod_\{i=j+1\}^\{t\}\\alpha_i\\big) k_j v_j^\\top$. Every past token keeps a nonzero weight, and the model can learn \uc0\u945  \u8776  1 to keep it forever. So the reach is unbounded too: it's the same bypass, just compressed. You could only force it bounded by resetting the state every w tokens, and then it's a worse version of SWA.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
SWA with window w:
\f1\b0  position t sees only j 
\f9 \uc0\u8712 
\f1  [t\uc0\u8722 w+1, t]. The reach is bounded and exact.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 So the decoder's mixer is SWA (plus short convs). The constraint forces this; it isn't a matter of taste. Linear attention can come back at scale inside the 
\f6\i core
\f1\i0 , where long reach is the point. That was already on the core's scale path.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

