\cf0 Each plan u_j already contains information the core retrieved from far back. A decoder that attends over 11 of them can combine them itself. That's IHN's F7 ("the decoder's cross-attention composed on its own") in miniature, and the recurrence would lose work to it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 The fix: a position may read only its own plan.
\f1\b0  Use the same trick as the encoder's L/G split, with three streams at each position t:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
T_t = tok_t
\f1\b0 : the encoder's token stream. It is read-only in the decoder and has no plan in it.\
\ls12\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
P_t
\f1\b0 : position t's plan, built from (u_\{j*(t)\}, \uc0\u265 _\{j*(t)+1\}). How P is built is Step 2.\
\ls12\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
D_t
\f1\b0 : the decoder's own stream, starting at D
\f8 \uc0\u8304 
\f1 _t = T_t. 
\f3\b Nothing ever reads D at another position.
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Each decoder layer does two things.\
The attention sublayer asks the question with the plan and looks up the answer in plain tokens:\uc0\u8232 $$x_t=\\mathrm\{GRRead\}(\{D_t, P_t\}),\\quad q_t = W_Q x_t,\\quad k_j=\\mathrm\{conv\}(W_K T)_j,\\ v_j=\\mathrm\{conv\}(W_V T)_j,\\quad j\\in[t-w+1,,t]$$\u8232 $$D_t \\leftarrow D_t + s_t, W_O\\Big(\\textstyle\\sum_j \\mathrm\{softmax\}
\f6\i j\\big(\\tfrac\{q_t\\cdot k_j\}\{\\sqrt\{d_h\}\}\\big), v_j \\odot \\sigma(W
\f1\i0 \\theta x_t)\\Big)$$\
The FFN sublayer is x_t = GRRead(\{D_t, P_t\}), then D_t 
\f2 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  D_t + s\'b7FFN(x_t).\
Unpacking the symbols:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The query q_t comes from the plan-aware stream. It encodes "what the plan wants from the local context", for example "the name that was introduced 30 tokens ago".\
\ls13\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The keys k_j and values v_j come only from T, so what gets retrieved is plain local tokens and never another position's plan.\
\ls13\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The sum is ordinary softmax attention over the window.\
\ls13\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\uc0\u963 (W_\u952  x_t) is the output gate, as in the encoder.\
\ls13\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
s_t is the write scale.\
\ls13\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
q gets 
\f3\b no
\f1\b0  short conv, because a conv over q would mix D_\{t\uc0\u8722 3..t\}, which carry earlier positions' plans.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Geometrically, q_t is a direction chosen by the plan. The attention finds the local tokens whose keys point that way and copies their values into position t's private stream.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 The two properties this buys:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
C3 holds exactly.
\f1\b0  D_t depends on P_t and on T in the window, and never on P_\{t'\} for t' \uc0\u8800  t.\
\ls14\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Reach doesn't grow with decoder depth.
\f1\b0  Every layer's keys come from T, never from D, so\uc0\u8232 $$\\text\{reach\}=63+(w-1)+(K-1)=73\\ \\text\{ for \} w=8,\\ K=4,$$\u8232 whether the decoder has 2 layers or 12. In a plain stack, reach grows by 10 per layer. That decoupling lets us choose depth for capacity without paying for it in bypass risk.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 The cost, stated honestly.
\f1\b0  Positions don't share decoder computation. Position t can't reuse the work position t\uc0\u8722 1 did while "spelling out" the plan. It has to recompute from its own offset in the chunk and the local tokens, which T_t contains. Whether that hurts is an empirical question, so the NCP-style plain stack stays as an arm.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs36 \cf0 3. The residual stream: gated residual, not depth routers\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 What IRC, Kimi AttnRes and Delta AttnRes solve is 
\f3\b dilution
\f1\b0 . After L residual adds, each layer's write is roughly 1/L of the stream, so deep layers can't find the early ones. Routing over depth fixes that. With a decoder of about 4 layers there's almost nothing to dilute. We measured it too: CDR, IRC and CRC routers all saturated and were causally inert (F2, +0.0005 to +0.008 nats).\
The gated-residual grammar also gives us something the routers can't: 
\f3\b read/write masks
\f1\b0 . Those are exactly what section 2 needs (D is written; T and P are read-only). It's also the grammar the encoder and the v2.1 core already use (X, Z read-only; S written), so all three modules speak one language.\
One required change: the read gate on P must have a floor, g_P = \'bd + \'bd\uc0\u963 (\'b7) 
\f9 \uc0\u8712 
\f1  (0.5, 1), so the only long-range route can't be switched off (encoder rule 6). Depth routers come back on the scale path once any module reaches 16 or more layers.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs36 \cf0 4. The output objective: NextLat yes, HiLP is already inside\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Why NextLat's belief state works, from scratch.
\f1\b0  Two conditions:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Next-token consistency:
\f1\b0  the head reads the next-token distribution off h_t exactly.\
\ls15\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Transition consistency:
\f1\b0  h_\{t+1\} is a function of (h_t, x_\{t+1\}) alone.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Given both, you can generate the entire future from h_t alone: sample x_\{t+1\} from the head, update h, repeat. So h_t is a 
\f3\b sufficient statistic
\f1\b0  of the past: a belief state. NTP alone doesn't force this, because attention can look back at raw tokens instead of compressing them.\
The implementation, for d = 1:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The prediction is a residual step: $\\hat h_\{t+1\} = h_t + f_\\psi(\\mathrm\{LN\}[h_t;\\ E x_\{t+1\}])$.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
f_\uc0\u968  is a 3-layer MLP.\
\ls16\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
E x_\{t+1\} is the next token's embedding, the "action".\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The regression loss is $\\mathcal L_h = \\mathrm\{SmoothL1\}(\\mathrm\{sg\}[h_\{t+1\}],\\ \\hat h_\{t+1\})$. It measures the distance between the predicted point and the true next point.\
\ls16\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The distillation loss is $\\mathcal L_\{KL\} = \\mathrm\{KL\}\\big(p^\{sg\}(\\cdot\\mid \\mathrm\{sg\}[h_\{t+1\}])\\ |\\ p^\{sg\}(\\cdot\\mid \\hat h_\{t+1\})\\big)$. It asks the prediction to agree with the true state 
\f6\i as the head sees it
\f1\i0 , through a frozen copy of the head.\
\ls16\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The ablations say both stop-gradients matter.\
\ls16\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
p_\uc0\u968  exists only in training and is discarded at inference.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 What it would do in our model.
\f1\b0  Here h_t = F(T_t, P_t). The whole past reaches h_t only through the plan. Consider the chunk boundary: going from t = 4n+2 to t+1 = 4n+3, the plan switches from u_\{n\uc0\u8722 1\} to u_n. For p_\u968  to predict h_\{t+1\}, it has to predict u_n from u_\{n\u8722 1\} plus the new tokens. So the NextLat gradient pushes 
\f3\b the plan
\f1\b0  toward being a belief state of the prefix, which is precisely the concept module's job.\
And it 
\f3\b cannot
\f1\b0  open a bypass, because the reach is bounded by construction. That's the payoff of making the bounds structural: auxiliary losses can shape representations, but they can't reroute information.\

\f3\b Evidence and cost:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In our own lab (PRISM), the NextLat + KL auxiliaries were the only consistent positive: 3 of 3 seeds.\
\ls17\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The paper shows strong gains on planning, path-star and countdown.\
\ls17\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
On language, perplexity at 1.3B was about 
\f3\b +0.03 nats worse
\f1\b0  on FineWeb-Edu and Wikitext (10.83 vs 10.52), better on LAMBADA, with +0.4 on downstream average at d = 2. That +0.03 is outside our \'b10.02 tie band.\
\ls17\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
It keeps about 83% of the baseline's training throughput.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 So it goes in as a gated arm: d = 1, \uc0\u955 _h = 1, \u955 _KL between 0.1 and 1, with stop-gradients on both terms, and the losses masked across document boundaries.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

