\cf0 The fix is also a simplification. Confinement only requires that nothing reads the decoder stream at 
\f6\i other
\f1\i0  positions. It doesn't require the plan to be a separate stream. So the simpler variant adds the plan into the private stream, exactly as NCP does (D
\f8 \uc0\u8304 
\f1  = tok + P), and keeps keys/values from 
\f4\fs26 tok
\f1\fs24  only. That makes it differ from the stack in exactly one line (where keys and values come from), with confinement and the 70-token reach still exact (unit tests pass). Training it on both seeds now.The decoder is designed and tested end to end, and every exact unit test passes. The long-range tests carry a value about 100 tokens (up to 117), past what the token path can reach. On those tests it matched the plain NCP-style decoder at 97\'9698%, while keeping the guarantees that decoder lacks. The test also caught one of my earlier ideas: the plan as a separate stream with its own gate learned in only 1 of 2 seeds, so I dropped it. The final design is simpler than what I proposed last turn.\
