\f3\b \cf0 One limit, upstream of the decoder:
\f1\b0  with 4 facts, each a 3-token value, both decoders stayed at chance for 1,500 steps. Probes show where it breaks:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls33\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The fact's concept vector carries its key at 94.5% but its first value token at only 39%.\
\ls33\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The core's output at the query carries nothing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 So retrieval in the core and how much the encoder can pack into one concept are the bottleneck, not the decoder. It's the concept-capacity risk (gate G-E1) the encoder spec already flagged.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 Caveats:
\f1\b0  everything ran on CPU at width 128, with 1\'962 seeds, synthetic tasks and a stand-in core. The mechanics and routing are verified; language quality isn't.\

